  "grouped_store_proof": [
    "Exact two-statement literal store plus positive-stride update; plain declared/context i64 private cursor, stable bound/step, exact integer payload types. Captures, address exposure, extra effects, debug and possible prefix mappings reject.",
    "Original condition executes before receiver capture. Zero iterations cause no owner-header read. Only private LOCAL slices, fixed FRAME/GLOBAL arrays and closed raw RegionArray receivers are admitted.",
    "The full conjunction proves 0<=cursor<exclusive_end<=u32 length, 0<stride<=UINT32_MAX, and widened base+end*width<=memory bytes. Guard arithmetic is nontrapping; invalid wrapped end values cannot pass the complete proof.",
    "cursor+3*stride<end proves four ordered stores. The following cursor+4*stride is below 2^33. Successful physical-span checks make i32 address conversions exact for all stores, including the last byte.",
    "For a raw owner, the entire possible write interval is disjoint from its whole HeaderLayout span. PackArrayView reads raw base/length without mode validation; every header byte therefore remains stable until the unchanged scalar tail. Encoded owners are rejected.",
    "The literal has the exact element type; raw Store truncation preserves the same low bits as scalar normalization followed by Store. Delaying the private cursor update until four nontrapping stores is unobservable: no callbacks, additional effects or exposed cursor exist.",
    "Guard failure and exhausted groups reach one original scalar while, preserving ordered partial writes, bounds/physical traps, abort payloads and final cursor. The shared suppression flag prevents recursive rematching."
  ],
  "byte_scan_proof": [
    "Exact equality-to-literal byte predicate, last=cursor then count++, and literal stride 1/2/4/8. Cursor, count and last are distinct private plain i64 locals; the bound aliases none. Only private LOCAL slices or fixed FRAME/GLOBAL arrays are admitted, never owners.",
    "Captured view and bound expressions have no memory effects or traps for admitted storage. Invalid or zero-trip inputs enter the unchanged scalar loop; no eager owner read is possible.",
    "The widened whole-span guard proves every byte of each 16-byte vector readable, including scalar-stride-skipped lanes. Unaligned loads are permitted. A group runs only when cursor+16<=exclusive_end.",
    "Byte equality and the mask select exactly offsets 0,step,...,15. popcnt is the number of matching scalar iterations; the highest set bit is their final matching index. Exact signed/unsigned byte contexts preserve equality of normalized literal bits.",
    "Nondebug i64 count addition is modular: adding popcnt equals the original number of increments modulo 2^64. Debug rejects, retaining checked overflow behavior. No count bound is required in the nondebug proof.",
    "Count/last updates may be reordered because the locals are distinct and private, all vector reads are nontrapping and no callback/effect can observe intermediate state. Last remains unchanged for an empty mask; cursor advances exactly 16 before the scalar tail."
  ],
  "integration": "ByteScan, GroupedStores and BoundedMerge share bounded fallback suppression. Patterns do not overlap. Prior merge changes are only the suppression-field rename; accepted merge arithmetic/emission is otherwise unchanged.",
